(* ============================================================ *)
(* Algebraic Operator ISA Grammar                               *)
(* The law surface of an executable operator.                   *)
(* ============================================================ *)

(* The Algebraic Operator ISA (AOI) is not an executor and not a policy.
   It is the layer that says which algebraic laws a declared operator obeys,
   so execution can decide whether an operation may be regrouped,
   reordered, parallelised, accumulated, inverted, or safely repeated.

       AIML / SRAI          select and redirect an operator
       MathML -> KAST       parse the mathematical expression
       Algebraic contract   validate types, identities, laws, effects
       XCFE + K'UHUL        admit and execute the operation
       Ch'en -> Xul         verify, then commit

   AOI != XCFE Policy != Fold Kernel != Execution.

   Three-valued laws are the core discipline:

       true   the law holds
       false  the law provably fails
       null   the law is NOT APPLICABLE

   null never means "unchecked". A unary operator such as SCORE has no
   associativity at all; the associativity that matters belongs to the
   binary operation that later combines the scalars. Collapsing null into
   "probably fine" is the defect this grammar exists to prevent.

   Mathematical associativity is NOT executable associativity. Real
   addition is associative; IEEE-754 float addition is not. A contract
   therefore carries a reproducibility policy in addition to its laws:
   regrouping is licensed only when both the law and the carrier agree.

   Unitality is a law, not a flag. An algebra is unital when a two-sided
   identity exists:

       1_A . x = x . 1_A = x

   Unital does not imply commutative, and associative does not imply
   commutative. Matrix multiplication is the standard witness: (AB)C = A(BC)
   and AI = IA = A, yet AB != BA in general. That combination is exactly what
   ordered K'UHUL transformation composition needs, so the ISA must be able to
   state "associative, unital, not commutative" as one contract.

   Bilinearity is a second, independent axis:

       (x+y).z = x.z + y.z ,  z.(x+y) = z.x + z.y ,  (ax).(by) = (ab)(x.y)

   Bilinearity licenses distributing a product over a sum. It does not license
   regrouping, and it does not survive normalization: cosine similarity is a
   derived metric, not an inner product, and does not inherit the algebra of
   the product it normalizes.

   The square-zero (trivial) extension A = K + V completes the picture. Give V
   the zero product, v.w = 0, and set

       (a,v)(b,w) = (ab, aw + bv)

   There is no vw term, yet A is associative, commutative, bilinear and UNITAL,
   because the identity 1_A = (1,0) comes entirely from K. V is an ideal whose
   square is zero, and every submodule of V is an ideal of A contained in V.

   Zero multiplication is NOT zero computation. (0,v).(0,w) = 0 says nothing
   about <v,w>, cos(v,w) or M.v: those are external bilinear forms and module
   actions owned by other contracts. The algebraic product is silent about
   them, and a runtime that confuses the two would let a representational
   algebra claim execution authority. *)

(* ============================================================ *)
(* 1. CONCRETE GRAMMAR — JSON SHAPE                             *)
(* ============================================================ *)

AlgebraRegistry ::= "{" RegistryMember ( "," RegistryMember )* "}" ;
RegistryMember  ::= IdKey
                  | VersionKey
                  | DescriptionKey
                  | AuthorityKey
                  | VocabularyKey
                  | StructuresKey
                  | OperatorsKey
                  | ReducersKey
                  | FoldDefaultsKey
                  | InvariantsKey
                  | ValidationKey ;

IdKey           ::= '"id"' ":" String ;
VersionKey      ::= '"version"' ":" String ;
DescriptionKey  ::= '"description"' ":" String ;
AuthorityKey    ::= '"authority"' ":" Object ;
ValidationKey   ::= '"validation"' ":" Object ;

AuthorityMember ::= GrammarSrcKey
                  | OperatorRegistryKey
                  | ImplementationsKey
                  | RuntimeTypesKey ;
GrammarSrcKey   ::= '"grammar"' ":" String ;
OperatorRegistryKey ::= '"operator_registry"' ":" String ;
ImplementationsKey ::= '"implementations"' ":" StringList ;
RuntimeTypesKey ::= '"runtime_types"' ":" String ;

VocabularyKey   ::= '"vocabulary"' ":" Vocabulary ;
Vocabulary      ::= "{" LawStatesKey "," ReproducibilityKey "," CarriersKey "}" ;
LawStatesKey    ::= '"law_states"' ":" Object ;
ReproducibilityKey ::= '"reproducibility"' ":" Object ;
CarriersKey     ::= '"carriers"' ":" CarrierTable ;

CarrierTable    ::= "{" CarrierEntry ( "," CarrierEntry )* "}" ;
CarrierEntry    ::= String ":" CarrierSpec ;
CarrierSpec     ::= "{" ExactKey ( "," NoteKey )? "}" ;
ExactKey        ::= '"exact"' ":" Boolean ;
NoteKey         ::= '"note"' ":" String ;

StructuresKey   ::= '"structures"' ":" StructureList ;
StructureList   ::= "[" Structure ( "," Structure )* "]" ;
Structure       ::= "{" StructureMember ( "," StructureMember )* "}" ;
StructureMember ::= StructureIdKey
                  | FamilyKey
                  | StructureDescKey
                  | LawsKey
                  | StructuralKey
                  | ProductImageKey
                  | BinaryOperationsKey ;
StructureIdKey  ::= '"id"' ":" StructureName ;
FamilyKey       ::= '"family"' ":" FamilyName ;
StructureDescKey ::= '"description"' ":" String ;
LawsKey         ::= '"laws"' ":" LawTable ;
StructuralKey   ::= '"structural"' ":" StructuralTable ;
ProductImageKey ::= '"product_image"' ":" ProductImage ;
BinaryOperationsKey ::= '"binary_operations"' ":" StringList ;

LawTable        ::= "{" ( LawEntry ( "," LawEntry )* )? "}" ;
LawEntry        ::= LawName ":" LawRequirement ;
LawRequirement  ::= "true" | "false" | "null" | '"*"' ;

StructuralTable ::= "{" ( StructuralEntry ( "," StructuralEntry )* )? "}" ;
StructuralEntry ::= StructuralName ":" Boolean ;

OperatorsKey    ::= '"operators"' ":" ContractList ;
ReducersKey     ::= '"reducers"' ":" ContractList ;
ContractList    ::= "[" Contract ( "," Contract )* "]" ;
Contract        ::= "{" ContractMember ( "," ContractMember )* "}" ;
ContractMember  ::= OperatorKey
                  | KindKey
                  | ContractDescKey
                  | AlgebraKey ;
OperatorKey     ::= '"operator"' ":" OperatorName ;
KindKey         ::= '"kind"' ":" ( '"operator"' | '"reducer"' ) ;
ContractDescKey ::= '"description"' ":" String ;
AlgebraKey      ::= '"algebra"' ":" AlgebraBlock ;

FoldDefaultsKey ::= '"fold_defaults"' ":" Object ;
InvariantsKey   ::= '"invariants"' ":" StringList ;

AlgebraBlock    ::= "{" ( AlgebraMember ( "," AlgebraMember )* )? "}" ;
AlgebraMember   ::= StructureKey
                  | CarrierKey
                  | ScalarFieldKey
                  | BinaryOpKey
                  | ProductImageKey
                  | ClosedKey
                  | IdentityKey
                  | AssociativeKey
                  | CommutativeKey
                  | IdempotentKey
                  | InvertibleKey
                  | DistributiveKey
                  | UnitalKey
                  | BilinearKey
                  | AnticommutativeKey
                  | PureKey
                  | DeterministicKey
                  | OrderSensitiveKey
                  | PhasePolicyKey
                  | ReproducibilityPolicyKey
                  | CanonicalGroupingKey
                  | AlgebraNoteKey ;

StructureKey    ::= '"structure"' ":" StructureName ;
CarrierKey      ::= '"carrier"' ":" CarrierName ;
ScalarFieldKey  ::= '"scalar_field"' ":" ( String | "null" ) ;
BinaryOpKey     ::= '"binary_operation"' ":" BinaryOpName ;
ClosedKey       ::= '"closed"' ":" Boolean ;
IdentityKey     ::= '"identity"' ":" ( String | Number | "null" ) ;
AssociativeKey  ::= '"associative"' ":" LawValue ;
CommutativeKey  ::= '"commutative"' ":" LawValue ;
IdempotentKey   ::= '"idempotent"' ":" LawValue ;
InvertibleKey   ::= '"invertible"' ":" LawValue ;
DistributiveKey ::= '"distributive"' ":" LawValue ;
UnitalKey       ::= '"unital"' ":" LawValue ;
BilinearKey     ::= '"bilinear"' ":" LawValue ;
AnticommutativeKey ::= '"anticommutative"' ":" LawValue ;
PureKey         ::= '"pure"' ":" Boolean ;
DeterministicKey ::= '"deterministic"' ":" Boolean ;
OrderSensitiveKey ::= '"order_sensitive"' ":" Boolean ;
PhasePolicyKey  ::= '"phase_policy"' ":" PhasePolicyName ;
ReproducibilityPolicyKey ::= '"reproducibility"' ":" ReproducibilityName ;
CanonicalGroupingKey ::= '"canonical_grouping"' ":" GroupingSpec ;
AlgebraNoteKey  ::= '"note"' ":" String ;

GroupingSpec    ::= "{" '"kind"' ":" GroupingName "," '"chunk"' ":" Integer "}" ;

LawValue        ::= "true" | "false" | "null" ;
StructureName   ::= '"none"' | '"scalar_arithmetic"' | '"monoid"'
                  | '"commutative_monoid"' | '"group"' | '"abelian_group"'
                  | '"semilattice_meet"' | '"semilattice_join"' | '"lattice"'
                  | '"ring"' | '"module"' | '"algebra"'
                  | '"associative_algebra"' | '"unital_associative_algebra"'
                  | '"nonassociative_algebra"' | '"inner_product_space"'
                  | '"square_zero_extension"' ;
FamilyName      ::= '"atomic"' | '"group_like"' | '"ring_like"'
                  | '"lattice_like"' | '"module_like"' | '"algebra_like"' ;
ProductImage    ::= '"none"' | '"carrier"' | '"scalar"' ;
PhasePolicyName ::= '"none"' | '"preserve"' | '"advance"' ;
ReproducibilityName ::= '"exact"' | '"deterministic_grouping"'
                  | '"implementation_defined"' | '"unspecified"' ;
GroupingName    ::= '"sequential"' | '"chunked"' | '"balanced"' | '"free"' ;
CarrierName     ::= String ;
BinaryOpName    ::= String ;
LawName         ::= '"associative"' | '"commutative"' | '"idempotent"'
                  | '"invertible"' | '"distributive"' | '"unital"'
                  | '"bilinear"' | '"anticommutative"' ;
StructuralName  ::= '"closed"' ;
OperatorName    ::= String ;
Integer         ::= JSON_Integer ;
String          ::= JSON_String ;
Number          ::= JSON_Number ;
Boolean         ::= JSON_Boolean ;
StringList      ::= "[" ( String ( "," String )* )? "]" ;
Object          ::= JSON_Object ;


(* ============================================================ *)
(* 2. ABSTRACT GRAMMAR — THE LAW ALGEBRA                        *)
(* ============================================================ *)

AlgebraADT      ::= "<" "operator:" OperatorName ","
                         "structure:" StructureName ","
                         "carrier:" CarrierName ","
                         "scalar_field:" ( CarrierName | "null" ) ","
                         "laws:" LawVector ","
                         "purity:" Purity ","
                         "phase:" PhasePolicyName ","
                         "reproducibility:" ReproducibilityName ">" ;

LawVector       ::= "(" "assoc:" LawValue "," "comm:" LawValue ","
                         "idem:" LawValue "," "inv:" LawValue ","
                         "dist:" LawValue "," "unit:" LawValue ","
                         "bilin:" LawValue "," "anticomm:" LawValue ")" ;

Purity          ::= "pure" | "impure" ;
Determinism     ::= "deterministic" | "nondeterministic" ;

TypeJudgment    ::= "|-" AlgebraADT ":" StructureFamily ;
StructureFamily ::= FamilyName ;

(* The derived execution permissions. Every one of them is a theorem over the
   declared laws, never an assumption over the operator's name. *)
Permission      ::= "regroup"
                  | "reorder"
                  | "swap_with_sign"
                  | "distribute"
                  | "elide_unit"
                  | "parallel"
                  | "repeat"
                  | "invert"
                  | "empty_fold"
                  | "phase_step" ;

RegroupDerivation   ::= "regroup"    "<=" "assoc = true" "AND" "pure = true"
                                      "AND" "reproducible(carrier)" ;
ReorderDerivation   ::= "reorder"    "<=" "regroup" "AND" "comm = true"
                                      "AND" "order_safe(carrier)" ;
SwapDerivation      ::= "swap_with_sign" "<=" "anticomm = true" "AND" "pure = true" ;
DistributeDerivation ::= "distribute" "<=" "bilin = true" "AND" "pure = true" ;
UnitDerivation      ::= "elide_unit" "<=" "unit = true" "AND" "pure = true" ;
ParallelDerivation  ::= "parallel"   "<=" "regroup" ;
RepeatDerivation    ::= "repeat"     "<=" "idem = true" "AND" "pure = true" ;
InvertDerivation    ::= "invert"     "<=" "inv = true" "AND" "pure = true" ;
EmptyFoldDerivation ::= "empty_fold" "<=" "unit = true" "AND" "pure = true" ;
PhaseDerivation     ::= "phase_step" "<=" "phase_policy = advance" "AND" "xcfe_admission" ;
PhasePreserve       ::= "phase_policy = preserve" "implies" "NOT phase_step" ;

Grouping        ::= Sequential | Chunked | Balanced | Free ;
Sequential      ::= "left_fold" "(" "identity" "," "x_1..x_n" ")" ;
Chunked         ::= "(" "chunk_1" ")" "op" "(" "chunk_2" ")" "op" "..." ;
Balanced        ::= "tree" "(" "x_1..x_n" ")" ;
Free            ::= "any_tree" "(" "permutation" "(" "x_1..x_n" ")" ")" ;

(* Product type contracts: the image of the binary operation decides whether an
   operator can be composed as a multiplication. *)
ProductType     ::= "V x V -> V" | "V x V -> R" | "V x R -> V" | "none" ;
AlgebraLaw      ::= ProductType "=" '"carrier"' implies Composable ;
InnerProductLaw ::= ProductType "=" '"scalar"' implies NotComposable ;


(* ============================================================ *)
(* 3. SEMANTIC INVARIANTS                                        *)
(* ============================================================ *)

A1  ::= law_value in {true, false, null} ;
A2  ::= null means NOT_APPLICABLE, never unchecked and never permitted ;
A3  ::= a structure's laws table is binding on every contract of that structure ;
A4  ::= '*' requires an applicable declaration: true or false, never null ;
A5  ::= commutative = true implies order_sensitive = false ;
A6  ::= associative = true does not imply commutative and does not license regroup ;
A7  ::= regroup requires associative = true and pure = true ;
A8  ::= regroup on a non-exact carrier requires reproducibility in {exact, deterministic_grouping} ;
A9  ::= reorder additionally requires commutative = true ;
A10 ::= repeat requires idempotent = true and pure = true ;
A11 ::= invert requires invertible = true and pure = true ;
A12 ::= empty_fold requires has_identity = true ;
A13 ::= effects containing propose_delta implies pure = false ;
A14 ::= product_image = carrier implies associative is applicable ;
A15 ::= inner_product_space has product_image = scalar and associativity not applicable ;
A16 ::= nonassociative_algebra requires associative = false explicitly ;
A17 ::= deterministic = false withholds every executable algebraic permission ;
A18 ::= lattice meet cannot widen authority: meet(A,B) <= A and meet(A,B) <= B ;
A19 ::= every SRAI operator resolves to exactly one algebra entry ;
A20 ::= the executable grouping is chosen from the contract, never from lexical position ;
A21 ::= mathematical associativity is not executable associativity ;
A22 ::= SCORE declares no binary law; its combiner does ;
A23 ::= unital = true iff identity names an element; unital = false means no unit exists; unital = null means no product ;
A24 ::= unital does not imply commutative; associative does not imply commutative ;
A25 ::= an identity operator preserves the phase; only phase_policy = advance crosses a phase boundary ;
A26 ::= bilinearity licenses distribution over addition, not regrouping; it does not survive normalization ;
A27 ::= anticommutativity licenses swapping operands only together with a sign flip ;
A28 ::= a derived metric does not inherit the algebra of the operation it normalizes ;
A29 ::= square_zero_extension binds associative, commutative, unital and bilinear, and binds invertible = false ;
A30 ::= zero multiplication is not zero computation: an internal product of zero says nothing about an external bilinear form ;
A31 ::= a representational algebra is not an executable fold: it organizes state and grants no execution authority ;
